---
// The documentation layout and not TestPageLayout: this page is about the
// fixtures, not one of them, so it keeps the sidebar.
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import { testPages } from '@data/testPages';
import Card from '@ui/Card.vue';

const checks = ['Does it use real Tailwind color names, or did it reach for <code>bg-primary</code>?', 'Do neutrals sit one rung from their background, and does each button carry the right <code>surface</code> for the card it is in?', 'Do all five accents stay at 300?', 'Is the default body size <code>text-sm</code>?', 'Does the dense inbox get a dense treatment, and the wizard a roomy one?', 'Do the empty, loading, and error states get the same care as the happy path?'];
---

<Layout title="Test Pages">
  <h1>Test Pages</h1>

  <p>
    Nine pages of real production markup pulled from the <code>voxie</code> app, stripped of every Tailwind class and filled with static test data. They render as raw semantic HTML. Nothing here is styled — that is the point.
  </p>

  <p>They were picked by layout archetype rather than by feature, so the set spans what the product actually has to lay out: a dense two-pane inbox, a wizard at the opposite density, tables that reflow to cards, a settings column, and a page collecting the states everything else falls into.</p>

  <h2>The pages</h2>

  <ul class="not-prose space-y-3">
    {
      testPages.map((page) => (
        <li class="leading-snug">
          <a
            href={page.href}
            class="text-sky-700 font-semibold hover:text-black"
          >
            {page.title}
          </a>
          <br />
          <span class="text-sm">{page.exercises}</span>
          <br />
          <code class="text-xs bg-slate-300/50 px-1 py-0.5 rounded-sm">{page.source}</code>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Running a trial</h2>

  <p>Point an agent at one page with a brief along these lines:</p>

  <Card padding="spacious">
    <p class="mt-0">Style src/pages/test-pages/dashboard.astro. It's real production markup with every class stripped.</p>

    <p>Read these first and treat them as binding: src/content/docs/foundations/color.mdx, foundations/typography.mdx, foundations/look-and-feel.mdx, components/button.mdx, components/card.mdx, foundations/page-structure.mdx.</p>

    <h3>Rules:</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Add classes freely. You may add wrapper elements and swap in existing components documented here e.g. a plain container for Card.</li>
      <li>Don't create new components.</li>
      <li>Don't remove or rename semantic elements, data-test attributes, or copy, and don't change the data.</li>
      <li>Don't touch _AppShell.astro. If you need something like a page background color, put it on the main content wrapper.</li>
      <li>When the docs don't answer something, make the call, but keep a running list of every gap you hit.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-0">Then self-review against the checklist in src/pages/test-pages/index.astro and report the gap list.</p>
  </Card>

  <h2>Review Checklist</h2>

  <ul>
    {checks.map((check) => <li set:html={check} />)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Resetting</h2>

  <p>
    These are fixtures, so they have to survive being styled. Note the commit before handing a page over; <code>git checkout -- src/pages/test-pages/</code> puts every page back to raw markup.
  </p>

  <p>
    The same brief, plus notes on how the markup was stripped, lives in <code>src/pages/test-pages/_README.md</code>.
  </p>
</Layout>
